<title>CANADA: Alberta, B.C. market regulators to cooperate.</title>
<headline>Alberta, B.C. market regulators to cooperate.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stock market regulators in Alberta and British Columbia signed a cooperation deal Monday aimed at strengthening securities enforcement.</p>
<p>The securities commissions of the two Canadian provinces said they were committed to improving the effectiveness and efficiency of their regulatory efforts.</p>
<p>Officials said the securities industries in the two provinces were similar with a focus on venture capital markets. The two commissions are the only ones in Canada that have been granted self-funding status and rule-making powers by their respective provincial governments.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314</p>
